<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Congress of Honduras</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Congress is the single-chamber legislature of Honduras, sitting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tegucigalpa">Tegucigalpa</a>. Under the constitution of 1982 its 128 deputies are elected by proportional representation for four-year terms. It played a central part in the crisis of 2009, when it endorsed the removal of President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-zelaya">Manuel Zelaya</a> and named its own president, Roberto Micheletti, as head of state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-congress-of-honduras.jpg" alt="National Congress of Honduras" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Congreso Nacional de Honduras · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_del_Congreso_Nacional_de_Honduras.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
